  "original_text": "INT. FAMILY HOUSE - MORNING\n\nAMAR\nI promised I would deliver the letter before noon.\n\nAmar folds the letter and puts it inside his cloth bag. His younger sister Meera watches him from the doorway.\n\nMEERA\nYou have been saying that since sunrise.\n\nEXT. MARKET ROAD - AFTERNOON\n\nAmar walks through the crowded road with the cloth bag over his shoulder. Meera catches up with him.\n\nMEERA\nThe bus has already left. Tell me what is really in that letter.\n\nAMAR\nIt is an apology. Father wrote it, but he could not bring himself to send it.\n\nINT. SMALL SHOP - EVENING\n\nSHOPKEEPER\nYou came a long way for a piece of paper.\n\nAmar removes the letter from his cloth bag and places it on the counter.\n\nAMAR\nThe paper is small. What it needs to repair is not.\n\n",
